{"step_index":303,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T21:52:25Z","thinking":"**Considering the Scope**\n\nI'm currently focused on defining the parameters of this project. The user's requirement for a VBA macro solution within the Excel file itself is clear. I'm noting the acceptance of the macro-enabled `.xlsm` file type. Now I am working to understand exactly what needs to go into the \"Needs Review\" column.\n\n\n**Defining Macro Implementation**\n\nNow I'm delving into the core functionality: row movement based on dropdown selection. If \"✅ مطابق\" is chosen, the row heads to the specified warehouse sheet; \"❌ غير مطابق\" redirects to the \"لم يُعثر عليه\" sheet. I need to make sure this transfers over any values. I need to think through the complexities with error handling.\n\n\n**Exploring Macro Automation**\n\nI've determined that direct Python-to-VBA generation isn't feasible, but there are workarounds. I'm prioritizing programmatic approaches. My current focus is on a template-based macro method. This entails creating a `.xlsm` template with the VBA code, which Python then populates with data. It looks like the user is asking for the VBA solution to be implemented and added, rather than the VBA code to be provided separately. I'm leaning toward this template strategy for a seamless solution.\n\n\n**Refining Automation Approach**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on a robust and reliable automation strategy. The initial idea of generating `.xlsm` directly has evolved. I've considered using `xlsxwriter` but realized that obtaining the `vbaProject.bin` file isn't straightforward. Instead, I'm leaning toward a combined approach. First I will write the VBA code in a text file. Then, I'm investigating a Python script that uses `win32com.client` to invisibly inject the code into the Excel workbook and save it. It will be implemented as a VBA solution. I'll write out the exact VBA code now!\n\n\n**Constructing Core VBA Code**\n\nNow I'm writing out the specific VBA code. I'm focusing on the `Worksheet_Change` event to trigger row movement. The logic is: When the \"القرار\" column (let's say it's Column A) changes: If it's \"❌ غير مطابق\", the row is copied to the \"لم يُعثر عليه\" sheet and then deleted from \"يحتاج مراجعة\". I'll be sure to include error handling. Also, I'll provide a separate `.vba` file to show the user and give instructions on how they can place it in a template file.\n\n\n**Implementing the Logic**\n\nI'm now integrating the core VBA logic for the row movement. The code includes checks for data validity and the correct cell change, specifically looking at changes in Column A. It grabs relevant details. If \"✅ مطابق\" is selected, the code will identify the warehouse sheet and move the row there. Error handling is built into the script.\n\n\n**Finalizing Row Movement**\n\nI've just finalized the VBA code that handles moving rows when \"✅ مطابق\" is selected. The code now correctly identifies the target warehouse sheet using its name, and writes the relevant data (item name, warehouse name, and \"تأكيد يدوي\" or confirmation) to the correct columns, now in 1,2, and 3. I've also implemented the row deletion from \"يحتاج مراجعة\" after the data is transferred. I'm satisfied with the logic.\n\n\n**Addressing the Integration**\n\nMy latest thought process is focused on a more user-friendly deployment. I recognize the limitations of directly injecting VBA with `openpyxl`. I've outlined a solution: Create a template Excel file with the VBA macro, and then use a Python script to populate this template with data, saving the result as the final file, which will have the implemented VBA code.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"' يرجى نسخ هذا الكود ووضعه داخل شيت \"يحتاج مراجعة\" في محرر الأكواد (Alt + F11)\n\nPrivate Sub Worksheet_Change(ByVal Target As Range)\n    On Error GoTo ErrorHandler\n    ' إيقاف الأحداث مؤقتاً عشان الكود ميكررش نفسه لما نمسح الصف\n    Application.EnableEvents = False\n    \n    ' التأكد إن التغيير حصل في العمود الأول (القرار) وإنه في خلية واحدة بس\n    If Not Intersect(Target, Me.Columns(\"A\")) Is Nothing And Target.Count = 1 Then\n        Dim decision As String\n        decision = Target.Value\n        \n        Dim reqName As String\n        Dim whName As String\n        Dim whSheetName As String\n        \n        ' قراءة البيانات من نفس الصف\n        reqName = Target.Offset(0, 1).Value ' اسم الصنف المطلوب\n        whName = Target.Offset(0, 2).Value  ' اسم المرشح\n        whSheetName = Target.Offset(0, 3).Value ' اسم المخزن\n        \n        ' تنظيف اسم المخزن عشان يطابق اسم الشيت (نفس الـ Logic بتاع البايثون)\n        whSheetName = Left(whSheetName, 31)\n        whSheetName = Replace(whSheetName, \"[\", \"_\")\n        whSheetName = Replace(whSheetName, \"]\", \"_\")\n        whSheetName = Replace(whSheetName, \":\", \"_\")\n        whSheetName = Replace(whSheetName, \"*\", \"_\")\n        whSheetName = Replace(whSheetName, \"?\", \"_\")\n        whSheetName = Replace(whSheetName, \"/\", \"_\")\n        whSheetName = Replace(whSheetName, \"\\\", \"_\")\n        \n        If decision = \"✅ مطابق\" Then\n            Dim wsTarget As Worksheet\n            On Error Resume Next\n            Set wsTarget = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(whSheetName)\n            On Error GoTo ErrorHandler\n            \n            If Not wsTarget Is Nothing Then\n                Dim lastRow As Long\n                lastRow = wsTarget.Cells(wsTarget.Rows.Count, \"A\").End(xlUp).Row + 1\n                \n                ' نقل البيانات لشيت المخزن\n                wsTarget.Cells(lastRow, 1).Value = reqName\n                wsTarget.Cells(lastRow, 2).Value = whName\n                wsTarget.Cells(lastRow, 3).Value = \"تأكيد يدوي (مراجعة)\"\n                \n                ' مسح الصف من شيت المراجعة\n                Target.EntireRow.Delete\n            Else\n                MsgBox \"خطأ: لم يتم العثور على شيت المخزن \" & whSheetName\n            End If\n            \n        ElseIf decision = \"❌ غير مطابق\" Then\n            Dim wsNotFound As Worksheet\n            Set wsNotFound = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"لم يُعثر عليه\")\n            \n            Dim lastRowNF As Long\n            lastRowNF = wsNotFound.Cells(wsNotFound.Rows.Count, \"A\").End(xlUp).Row + 1\n            \n            ' نقل البيانات لشيت غير الموجود\n            wsNotFound.Cells(lastRowNF, 1).Value = reqName\n            wsNotFound.Cells(lastRowNF, 2).Value = \"مرفوض يدوياً\"\n            \n            ' مسح الصف من شيت المراجعة\n            Target.EntireRow.Delete\n        End If\n    End If\n    \nErrorHandler:\n    Application.EnableEvents = True\nEnd Sub\n","Description":"VBA Macro code to handle auto-moving rows based on dropdown selection in Excel","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\vba_macro.txt","toolAction":"Creating a text file containing the VBA Macro code","toolSummary":"Create VBA code file"}}]}
